enforcement: |
  The reinvest rule is now checked, not just stated. tools/check-drift.sh check
  (i) compares every submodule copy of schema_lint.py (and unwrap-prose.py)
  against the hub's, so a fork can no longer diverge unnoticed. It found two on
  the day it shipped.
notes: |
  2026-08-09 audit of the vendored copy:
  - tools/schema_lint.py is byte-identical to upstream HEAD (ce09aeb). The
    recorded upstream-commit said 04b0980, which was accurate when vendored but
    stale afterwards: 04b0980 was the last commit to TOUCH the linter, not the
    upstream HEAD. Recording the commit the file came from is only useful if it
    is the commit you can diff against, so `verified:` is now tracked too.
  - The vendored templates differ from upstream only by prose reflow (the fleet's
    one-paragraph-per-line rule). That is deliberate local adaptation, not drift.
  - Known gap: the hub vendors this linter to ~40 repos with NO local test
    coverage. Upstream has a 60-test suite that is not pulled in, so a re-vendor
    is currently verified only by the hub's own pyramid linting clean. Pulling
    the suite in (or running it against the vendored copy in CI) is the obvious
    next step.
  - Open upstream: bamr87/SCHEMA#4 fixes a real bug found by this audit — a
    schema that registers its own `SCHEMA.md` row was reported as missing that
    file. Re-vendor once it merges.
